NAME
    cat - copy file or input bytes

SYNOPSIS
    cat [-AbEnstTuv] [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
    Copies each file to standard output in argument order. With no file,
    copies standard input. A FILE of - also selects standard input. Processing
    state continues across operands, as though their bytes were concatenated.
    Reads are bounded by the mounted filesystem and shell stream limits.
    At an interactive prompt standard input is the session terminal: cat copies
    each typed line, ends at Ctrl-D, and reports cancellation at Ctrl-C. Use -u
    to write each line as it is read rather than aggregating it. See man sh.

OPTIONS
    -A  Show nonprinting bytes, line ends, and tabs; equivalent to -vET.
    -b  Number nonempty output lines, overriding -n.
    -e  Show nonprinting bytes and mark each line end with $; equivalent to -vE.
    -E  Mark each line end with $.
    -n  Number every output line.
    -s  Replace each run of repeated blank lines with one blank line.
    -t  Show nonprinting bytes and render tabs as ^I; equivalent to -vT.
    -T  Render tabs as ^I.
    -u  Write without the 512-byte output aggregation buffer.
    -v  Render control and high-bit bytes visibly using ^ and M- notation.

    Options may be combined. -- ends option parsing.
